# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sur — environment configuration
#
# EVERY VARIABLE IS OPTIONAL. The JioSaavn API is unauthenticated, so there are
# no secrets and the app boots with an empty environment. Copy to `.env` only if
# you want to override a default.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port for the LOCAL dev API server (server.ts). Ignored on Vercel, which
# invokes the exported app directly instead of binding a port.
# Must match the proxy target in vite.config.ts if you change it.
API_PORT=3001

# Upstream JioSaavn endpoint. Override to point at a mock/fixture server.
SAAVN_API_BASE=https://www.jiosaavn.com/api.php

# Per-request upstream timeout in milliseconds. Keep comfortably below Vercel's
# default function timeout (10s) so a slow upstream produces a clean 504 rather
# than being killed mid-response by the platform.
UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# CORS allowlist. Only relevant in local dev, where Vite (5173) and Express
# (3001) are different origins; in production both are same-origin behind
# Vercel's rewrites. Set to a specific origin to tighten.
CORS_ORIGIN=*

# Set automatically by Vercel. Locally, leaving this unset enables verbose
# error messages in API responses; `production` suppresses them.
# NODE_ENV=development
